-- title:
--   Equal supports and degrees force equal Hecke correspondences
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $q,q'$ and a field $F_0$ that is an algebra over $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and satisfies `IsCurveOver`, i.e. every nonzero element has a degree-zero divisor of orders, every place has residue field finite over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\Omega_{F_0/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ is free of rank one. Let $\mathbb T,\mathbb T'$ be two pieces of tower data over $F_0$ in the sense of `HeckeTower.TowerData`: for each prime $\ell$ with $\ell\neq q,q'$ a field $F_\ell$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a curve in the above sense and essentially of finite type, together with two $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra maps $\varphi_{\ell,0},\varphi_{\ell,1}\colon F_0\to F_\ell$, each module-finite and integral. Assume: (i) for every such $\ell$ and every place $P$ of $F_0$ the divisors $(\varphi_{\ell,1})_*(\varphi_{\ell,0})^*[P]$ and $(\varphi'_{\ell,1})_*(\varphi'_{\ell,0})^*[P]$ have the same support; (ii) for every arrow $(\ell,i)$ the ranks $\operatorname{finrankAlong}$ of $F_\ell$ over $F_0$ along $\varphi_{\ell,i}$ and of $F'_\ell$ along $\varphi'_{\ell,i}$ agree; (iii) for every $\ell$ the subfield of $F'_\ell$ generated by the images of $\varphi'_{\ell,0}$ and $\varphi'_{\ell,1}$ is everything. Then for every such $\ell$ and every divisor $D$ of $F_0$, $(\varphi_{\ell,1})_*(\varphi_{\ell,0})^*D = (\varphi'_{\ell,1})_*(\varphi'_{\ell,0})^*D$.
--
--   This upgrades an agreement of fibre supports to an equality of the push–pull (Hecke) correspondences attached to two towers of curves over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the form in which correspondences are compared in the Čerednik–Drinfeld descent step. It is used in the construction of descent intertwining data from a rigid oriented moduli witness, where only supports of fibres are directly available.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_HeckeTower_correspondence_eq_of_support_eq_of_finrankAlong_eq.lean

